---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, ADSENSE_CLIENT } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description={`The privacy policy for ${SITE_TITLE}: what Google Analytics, Google AdSense, Google Fonts and our host receive when you visit, and how to opt out.`}
	pubDate={new Date('June 18 2026')}
	updatedDate={new Date('October 6 2026')}
>
	<p>
		{SITE_TITLE} (spokdom.com, "this site") is a read-only review blog. There are no accounts,
		logins, comments, or contact forms. The only way the operator receives your name or contact
		details directly is if you choose to send an email. Opening a page does, however, send some
		information to the third-party services listed below, so this page states exactly what goes where.
	</p>

	<h2>1. Who runs this site</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Operator: Sungbin (individual, independent)</li>
		<li>Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:yangsungbin77@gmail.com">yangsungbin77@gmail.com</a></li>
	</ul>

	<h2>2. If you email us</h2>
	<p>
		If you email us, we use your address, name (if shown), and message only to reply and to fix
		articles. We don't share it with anyone. To have it deleted, ask at the same address.
	</p>

	<h2>3. Visitor statistics — Google Analytics 4</h2>
	<p>
		Every page loads Google Analytics 4 (GA4) so we can see which articles are read. GA4 sets cookies
		(such as <code>_ga</code>) and sends Google the page address, the referring site, browser and device
		type, and an approximate location derived from your IP address. We only see aggregated reports
		that don't identify individuals.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Opt out: install the
			<a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>,
			or block cookies in your browser.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>4. Advertising — Google AdSense</h2>
	{
		ADSENSE_CLIENT ? (
			<p>This site loads Google AdSense code and may show Google ads.</p>
		) : (
			<p>
				This site does not show ads or load advertising code right now. We plan to apply for Google
				AdSense. If ads are added, the following will apply, and this page will be updated.
			</p>
		)
	}
	<p>
		When AdSense code runs, Google and its partners may use cookies or similar identifiers to show ads
		based on your visits to this and other websites, to measure ad views and clicks, and to prevent
		fraud.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			How Google uses information from sites that use its services:
			<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>
		</li>
		<li>
			How Google uses advertising cookies:
			<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google advertising technologies</a>
		</li>
		<li>
			Turn off personalized ads:
			<a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a>.
			You can opt out of other vendors' personalized ads at
			<a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		If you turn off personalized ads you may still see ads, based on things like the page you're
		reading or your general location.
	</p>
	<p>
		Visitors in the European Economic Area, the UK, and Switzerland must be asked for consent before
		Google advertising and analytics cookies are used. We have not yet set up a consent management
		tool; when one is in place, we will describe it here. Until then, you can refuse these cookies with
		your browser's cookie-blocking settings.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Other services your browser connects to</h2>
	<p>These services receive your IP address and browser information when a page loads.</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosts and delivers the site, and processes access logs for security and reliability.</li>
		<li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — delivers the heading and code fonts (fonts.googleapis.com, fonts.gstatic.com).</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>6. Affiliate links</h2>
	<p>
		Some links may be affiliate links. If you click one and sign up or buy, we may earn a commission at
		no extra cost to you, and the vendor may set its own tracking cookie under its own privacy policy.
		This never changes a verdict.
	</p>

	<h2>7. External links</h2>
	<p>
		Articles link to vendor pricing pages and other sources. We're not responsible for those sites'
		privacy practices, so please check their own policies.
	</p>

	<h2>8. Refusing or deleting cookies</h2>
	<p>
		You can block or delete cookies in your browser's privacy settings (Chrome, Safari, Edge, Firefox,
		and others). Every article on this site still works with cookies blocked.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Retention</h2>
	<p>
		The only data we keep ourselves is email you send us, which we stop using once your question or
		correction is handled. Retention of GA4 and advertising data follows Google's settings and policies.
	</p>

	<h2>10. Children</h2>
	<p>This site is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect children's personal information.</p>

	<h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>
		When the services we use change, we update this page and the "Updated" date at the top. Questions?
		See the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
